### Fieldkit 2.1 (built staged beside 2.0; released as tag v2.1)
- Chat: one path (nova/chat.py) with SELF/NOW first, RULES (+ voice rule), GRAMMAR_V2, read-only hunt.
  Uses qwen3:8b ctx 8192 think:false. Guards: speak tags, ids, unrelated commands, action claims, voice line.
- SELF v2.1: version 2.1, a commands line with numeric ids, a directives line. NOW: thermal from the latest
  reading only, age-stamped; TASK lines from task-stimulus.
- GUI rewrite: read-only (one mode=ro connection; no workforce upsert, no palace writes; cached scandir),
  working Send/quick keys, the [:64] fix, show_media, hidden dead controls, worker-thread streaming + Cancel,
  health strip, WHAT NOVA KNOWS panel, PROPOSALS panel; actions go through the daemon command inbox.
- Scheduler v2: job table, priority, GPU classes + lock (one heavy at a time), backoff, run-now, command
  inbox executed by the daemon, task-stimulus job (HIL proposals only). Restart-safe next run.
- Gates: net allowlist (empty = refuse) on web/crawl; drain only approved URLs; chat scope + ack;
  governor fail-closed when enforcing plus `report` dry-run (enforce stays false); RAG judge fail-closed;
  chamber auto-promote off (proposal only).
- Self-improve loop: propose → review → approve → apply (sandbox marker only) → verify → PROOF.json.
- Disk: retention config + dry-run report; the daemon no longer deletes TTS wavs (maintain reports instead).
- Paths: nova/paths.py; hardcoded user paths removed from 11 modules (docs_ingest, msg, watson, whi,
  hands/paint, report_db_contents, homestead, tutorial, avatar_display, novadiary, tts_gui_tiles) + leash.
- Staged guard: a STAGED marker blocks the daemon/launch unless NOVA_HOME is a listed scratch home.
- Tests: 59 pass on the Windows build host (selfknow + v2.1 + GUI acceptance; 46 pass / 13 skip on Linux without PySide6), and both 2.0 smoke suites pass 8/8.
- Sim (qwen3:8b, 3 seeds, 12 prompts): v2.0 had 19/36 fabricated with speak tags on 36/36;
  v2.1 had 0/39 fabricated with speak tags on 0/39. Details are in the build report.
